     --33      Same as --oo nnffssvv33

     --DD      Same as --oo ddeeaaddtthhrreesshh

     --II      Same as --oo rreeaaddddiirrssiizzee=⟨_v_a_l_u_e⟩

     --LL      Same as --oo nnoolloocckkdd

     --NN      Same as --oo nnoorreessvvppoorrtt

     --PP      Use a reserved socket port number.  This flag is obsolete, and
             only retained for compatibility reasons.  (For the rare case
             where the client has a trusted root account but untrustworthy
             users and the network cables are in secure areas this does help,
